status  [green] Built 2 parts, RangeBox_r2_Layout, RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier and RangeBox_r2.SLDASM, reusing the 4 parts already built; no interference between the gears in any mode, where they stand. Its turning gears are mated to turn in each of its 3 modes, one configuration each (H, N and L), and SolidWorks reports no mate in error in any of them: it opens in H; to switch mode, double-click another mode's configuration in SolidWorks' ConfigurationManager. Drag Sun in SolidWorks and the rest of its train follow. RangeSlv slides along Output, to its place in each mode. The 3 copies of Planet turn on Carrier, and RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier holds Carrier's axes and planes only: a plate and pins are yours to add. Ring stays fixed where it is placed: its shaft does not turn. A turn you give the gears in one mode can show in other modes, so a dog can stand across its sleeve in another; to put the gears back there, press Update SolidWorks with that mode showing. 1 thing to do by hand: Assign a material to each of the 2 parts; the build leaves it unset. RangeBox.SLDASM is not open in SolidWorks, and Gear Generator reads it then only when it and every file it uses were last saved by this SolidWorks (a file saved since on another SolidWorks, or one not found or not read, is not read), so nothing of yours was carried; as read at 15:56, your Chain-1, Sprocket-3, Sprocket-4, 14 other components and 31 mates stay in RangeBox.SLDASM, and your User Keyway Sketch and User Keyway stay in Gear_m1.25_N29, which Sun's new part replaces; RangeBox_r2 has none of them, nor anything added since.
